  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "The chase moves upward",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Jing Hua climbed 241 places to 34th on Wednesday’s ARC-AGI-3 public board, adding 4.23 points since the previous evening close to reach 35.32. Juyong gained 3.72 points and rose 140 places to 31st at 35.55. Neither has reached the gold line of 37.18, but both have moved into a much stronger position in the chasing field."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Two leaders, a narrow gap",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs holds first at 68.91, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 67.49. Their scores are unchanged against the previous evening comparison, leaving Tufa’s advantage at 1.42 points. The nearest challenger, mtg, is third at 45.00. Dries Smit’s verified driessmit1 account remains on Tufa’s current six-account ARC-3 roster; Chen’s entry lists threerabbits. Tonight’s GPU icebreaker and two rabbits continue the paper’s friendly illustrated race. The machine and five spiders are editorial fantasy, not hardware evidence or a roster count."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The top ten stays crowded",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0",
        "person-darragh-hanley-identity-0",
        "person-elad-sarafian-identity-0",
        "person-gal-kaplun-identity-0",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-identity-0",
        "person-yeyin-zhu-identity-0",
        "person-richard-csaky-identity-0",
        "person-vineeth-sai-varikuntla-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "NVARC3 is fourth at 43.94, just 0.30 ahead of the last dance 🕺 in fifth. NVARC3’s result belongs to the observed six-person team: Jean-François Puget, Darragh Hanley, Elad Sarafian, Gal Kaplun, Ivan Sorokin and Yeyin Zhu. Artificial Agency Lab occupies eighth at 41.74, after an overnight observed score event from 38.62. Its current roster lists cmechevalier and Richard Csaky. That puts it 0.23 behind seventh-place Son & Mark & Ronen. ARC Slayers and Vineeth Sai Varikuntla complete the top ten at 41.19 and 40.09."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Gold has little room to spare",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-14-0757-arc-3-mikelou1-reaches-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-14-1005-arc-3-harsh-patel-saket-poswal-climb"
      ],
      "text": "The morning wire reported mikelou1’s move into provisional gold; the evening board still places the entry 17th at 37.27, only 0.09 above the cutoff. Md Boktiar Mahbub Murad is first outside the 18 gold places, in 19th at 37.12. Harsh Patel and Saket Poswal’s large morning moves remain consequential: their observed score events added 10.14 and 7.25 points, respectively. Tonight they stand 47th at 33.87 and 45th at 33.94. Those events are dated moves, not fresh gains since this morning’s filing. Snowiers adds another substantial evening-to-evening climb, up 185 places to 43rd with 34.04. All public medal positions remain provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A model result beyond the team race",
      "sourceIds": [
        "dispatch-2026-10-14-afternoon-haiku-55-results",
        "social-2110417867288039864",
        "social-2110459241316430266"
      ],
      "text": "ARC Prize’s Wednesday Haiku 5.5 announcement presents a sharp divide: 61.3% on ARC-AGI-2, but 0.45% on ARC-AGI-3 with the Standard harness and 2.82% with the Provider Adapter. The paper’s commissioned afternoon report develops those separate evaluation conditions and the unfinished ARC-2 max-reasoning run. These organizer model tests are separate from Kaggle team standings. In another evaluation thread, Matt Mazur says Baseten serves the original DeepSeek V4.1 Flash checkpoint, with its native fp8 and mxfp4 experts and no additional quantization. That is a testing clarification, not a new team score or an independently reproduced provider comparison."
    }
